le  who are using fentanyl and that's when  people need human connection the most I  have hope  I believe in recovery I don't believe  addicts all die I believe people recover  and I have hope I thought that if I lost  the eye I wouldn't have hope anymore and  yet I still have hope and that I would  help anybody who needed help illicit  fentanyl is just the latest wave in the  opioid crisis in a country with 5% of  the world's population but using 85% of  the world's opioids and a seemingly  ready supply to meet the demand  Greg Milam Sky News
 

